TITLE:: MaxxedBeats Assistant
summary:: Using the MaxxedBeats AI music assistant window
categories:: Assistant
related:: Classes/MaxxedBeats, Classes/ChaosOsc

SECTION:: Opening the window

Evaluate code::MaxxedBeats.gui:: in SCIDE. The window has four tabs:
strong::Compose::, strong::Variations::, strong::Keys & Privacy::, and
strong::Usage::. The project, the strong::Choose your DJ:: selector, the status
line, errors, and confirmation requests are always visible at the top.

SECTION:: Choose your DJ

Pick a provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, or the offline mock) and one of its models.
The window always shows the explicit provider id and model id that the next
request will use. Press strong::Refresh models:: to fetch the provider's current
model list. Models the assistant cannot use are labelled strong::unavailable::.
If your saved model disappears, it is shown as strong::UNAVAILABLE:: and requests
are blocked until you choose another model: MaxxedBeats never switches provider
or model on its own. If a refresh fails, the cached list stays visible and is
labelled as possibly stale.

SECTION:: API keys, privacy, and cost

On strong::Keys & Privacy:: you can save or replace, validate, and remove a key
for each provider independently. Keys are kept in the operating system's
credential store (macOS Keychain, Windows Credential Manager, Linux Secret
Service). Key entry is masked; keys are never shown, logged, or written to
settings or project files. Typed or pasted characters are appended; use
strong::Clear:: and paste again to correct a key.

Your prompt, the conversation, and only the project files you select under
strong::Context files:: are sent to the provider you chose. Requests may incur
charges on your provider account. Credits are an informational estimate
(100 credits per estimated US$1), not a balance or bill. When pricing is
missing or stale, USD and credits are labelled unavailable or stale and never
shown as zero.

SECTION:: Composing

NUMBEREDLIST::
## Open a project folder (strong::Choose...:: or type a path and press strong::Open::).
## Select context files, type a prompt, and press strong::Send to DJ::. strong::Cancel:: stops a running request.
## Review the proposed musical plan and the diff. Nothing has been written yet.
## strong::Approve and apply...:: asks for confirmation, saves a backup, and writes the files. strong::Reject:: discards the proposal. strong::Undo last apply...:: restores the most recent backup.
## strong::Render...:: asks for confirmation, then renders the chosen entry file offline in a separate sclang/scsynth process to a new WAV under code::renders/::. The result shows the file, format, and audio checks.
## strong::Play preview:: plays the rendered WAV on your running server (boot it with code::s.boot::); strong::Reveal file:: shows it in your file browser.
::

SECTION:: Variations

Start a variation session with a prompt and a candidate limit (1 to 4). Each
candidate is kept in an isolated session folder with its code, seed, settings,
render, and checks. strong::Stop:: ends the session early. strong::Audition
selected:: plays a candidate; strong::Apply selected...:: asks for confirmation
before replacing the project files (with a backup).

SECTION:: Troubleshooting

LIST::
## strong::"missing classes":: — re-run code::python3 scripts/install_maxxedbeats.py:: and recompile the class library.
## strong::No API key / auth errors:: — save or validate the key on strong::Keys & Privacy::.
## strong::Model unavailable:: — press strong::Refresh models:: and choose a listed model.
## strong::Play fails:: — boot the server with code::s.boot::; the WAV file is already rendered.
::
